From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: Keep connected haptics on endpoint churn

Opening a game's controller-speaker stream can temporarily remove and recreate
the corresponding PipeWire-Pulse endpoint.  Treating that endpoint addition as
a physical controller replacement closes an established raw ALSA haptic PCM
and moves it to the reappearing PipeWire node, which stops DualSense haptics.

Keep a registered haptic PCM on its existing path while ALSA still reports it
connected.  A real unplug changes the PCM to DISCONNECTED (or invalidates it
from the write path), so a later controller endpoint can still retarget the
Windows stream to the newly connected physical device.
---
 dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -3062,8 +3062,17 @@ static HRESULT pulse_retarget_dualsense_haptic_stream_path(struct pulse_stream
 {
+    snd_pcm_state_t state;
     char *path;
     HRESULT hr;
 
     if (!stream->dualsense_haptic_registered)
         return S_FALSE;
+    if (stream->haptic_pcm &&
+            (state = snd_pcm_state(stream->haptic_pcm)) != SND_PCM_STATE_DISCONNECTED)
+    {
+        TRACE("Keeping connected Sony controller haptic stream %p on %s during endpoint churn "
+                "(PCM state %s).\n", stream, debugstr_a(stream->haptic_alsa_path),
+                snd_pcm_state_name(state));
+        return S_FALSE;
+    }
     if (!(path = strdup(target)))
         return E_OUTOFMEMORY;
